nities had been ravaged by \nfloods, fires, tornadoes, or other dis­\nasters; and\nWHEREAS the Red Cross stands at \nthe side of our troops wherever they are \nstationed throughout the world, and also \nprovides invaluable assistance to those \nwar veterans who are still disabled or \nare maladjusted to civilian life; and \nWHEREAS, in order to help meet a \ngrowing post-war need, which would be \nmultiplied in the event of a national \ne","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_10037.txt","sha256":"6f541f782aeb640848ca67ea1cd0adedc983d57059441f8893360b490577fb7a","source":{"line":535,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"0aae81755039605843ad81057f43373067a518af93126ac0c65f53f36a33bcf5"}}]}
